### PAGE 6: APPOINTMENT BOOKING — /book-appointment

This is one of the most important pages of the website.

Build a professional, easy-to-use appointment booking experience.

STEP 1: SELECT A SERVICE
Allow patients to select an available dental service or consultation type.

STEP 2: SELECT A DENTIST
Allow selection of a preferred dentist or an option such as "First Available", if supported.

STEP 3: SELECT DATE AND TIME
Display available appointment slots based on actual configured clinic hours, dentist schedules, appointment durations, blocked periods, and existing bookings.

STEP 4: ENTER PATIENT DETAILS
Collect only the information necessary for booking, such as:

- Full name.
- Email address.
- Phone number with country code.
- New or returning patient status.
- Selected service.
- Preferred dentist.
- Appointment date and time.
- Optional accessibility or scheduling request.
- Required privacy acknowledgment.

Avoid collecting detailed medical histories or sensitive clinical information through a general-purpose booking form.

STEP 5: REVIEW AND CONFIRM
Display a clear booking summary and allow patients to verify their selections.

STEP 6: CONFIRMATION
After the backend successfully accepts the appointment, display a confirmation page with the booking reference and next steps.

Booking functionality must include:

- Server-side validation.
- Accurate availability checks.
- Time-zone-aware scheduling.
- Double-booking prevention.
- Database persistence.
- Appointment status tracking.
- Rescheduling and cancellation according to clinic policy.
- Email confirmation when configured.
- SMS reminders when a suitable provider is configured.
- Clear error, loading, and success states.

Do not show unavailable time slots. Prevent two patients from booking the same dentist and time when the schedule does not permit it.

Do not claim that an appointment is confirmed until the backend has successfully reserved the slot. If staff approval is required, label the booking as "Pending Confirmation".

Provide an alternative phone contact method if online booking is temporarily unavailable.

